1. Create a folder git_learning and initialize a Git repository.
mkdir git_learning
cd git_learning
git init

2. Create index.html and styles.css. Stage and commit them with the message "Initial project setup".
touch index.html styles.css
echo "sample content" > index.html
git add .
git commit -m "Initial project setup"

3. Create a file named .env and a .gitignore file. Configure the ignore file so that Git stops tracking all .log files.
touch .env .gitignore
echo "*.log" > .gitignore
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Added .gitignore"

4. Run a status check to prove the log file is invisible to Git.
touch sample.log
git status

Branching
1. Create and switch to a new branch named feature-about.
git checkout -b feature-about

2. Add an about.html file. Commit it.
touch about.html
git add about.html
git commit -m "added about.html"

3. Switch back to main and merge feature-about into it.
git branch -m master main
git checkout main
git merge feature-about

4. Intentionally delete the content of index.html. Use a Git command to restore the file to its last committed state without making a new commit.
echo "" > index.html
git restore index.html

5. In index.html create a h1 tag and add "Git learning".
echo "<h1>Git learning</h1>" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "index.html v1"

6. In same file edit the that h1 tag to "Done with git".
echo "<h1>Done with git</h1>" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "index.html v2"

7. Now i want the Git learning again, Use git revert to undo that commit by creating a "correction" commit.
git revert HEAD
git add index.html
git commit -m "correction"

Conflicts:
1. While on main, change the <h1> tag in index.html to "Learning GIT". Commit it.
echo "<h1>Learning git</h1>" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "index.html v3"

2. Create a branch fix-title from the previous commit. Change that same <h1> tag to "Completed the git". Commit it.
git checkout -b fix-title
echo "<h1>Completed the git</h1>" > index.html
git add index.html
git commit -m "index.html in fix-title branch"

3. Merge fix-title into main. Manually resolve the conflict in the editor and finalize the merge.
git checkout main
git merge fix-title
<<<<HEAD
Learning git
==========
Completed the git
>>>>>>fix-title

git add index.html
git commit -m "Merged conflicts"

